1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,587
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:06,673
[gunshots]

3
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:07,966
[gun clicks, fires]

4
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,677
[whoosh, slashing sounds]

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,679
[machine gun fire]

6
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,681
[machine gun fire continues]

7
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:15,765
[single gunshot]

8
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:20,395
[rapid gunfire]

9
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,397
[echoing blast]

10
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,107
[rapid gunfire]

11
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:25,942
[blade whooshing]

12
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,486
[tense music builds]

13
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:29,696
[blade whooshing]

14
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,242
[Arnaldo] <i>Thank you</i>
<i>for your loyal service.</i>

15
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:35,827
[gunshot]

16
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:39,039
[Julio] <i>Now, where is that witch,</i>
<i>Helena Montoya?!</i>

17
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:40,665
<i>I am going to kill her!</i>

18
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:42,751
<i>And if she survives, I'll kill her again.</i>

19
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,299
-[Camia] <i>Lily, it's an ambush!</i>
-[Helena] <i>Shoot them, baby girl!</i>

20
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:51,176
<i>-Shoot them!</i>
<i>-Mama!</i>

21
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:53,970
-[screams]
-[gunfire]

22
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:57,390
[Julio] <i>This is your destiny.</i>

23
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:58,933
<i>You know why?</i>

24
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:02,187
<i>It's because you messed</i>
<i>with the wrong Ardiente.</i>

25
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:03,730
<i>You messed with me.</i>

26
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>Mama!</i>

27
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:11,279
[Julio] <i>Lily Cruz was the one</i>
<i>who planted the bomb</i>

28
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,781
<i>in your mother's ambulance.</i>

29
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:16,576
<i>Lily Cruz was the one who killed her.</i>

30
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:20,747
<i>Did you hear that, Mama?</i>
<i>Papa said he'd avenge you.</i>

31
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:22,999
<i>My father made so many mistakes.</i>

32
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:27,462
<i>But on his behalf, I hope</i>
<i>one day you can forgive him.</i>

33
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:29,088
<i>I can't forgive him</i>

34
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:31,174
<i>because he's the reason this all started.</i>

35
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:37,055
<i>Raul saved me, Lily. I'm grateful to Raul.</i>

36
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:40,099
<i>So, we should try to forgive him.</i>

37
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,393
<i>I'm turning myself in.</i>

38
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:46,606
<i>I will pay for my crimes,</i>
<i>so I can be worthy of your love.</i>

39
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:48,608
<i>I hope you can wait for me, Camia.</i>

40
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:49,984
<i>I'll wait for you, Damian.</i>

41
00:01:50,401 --> 00:01:52,862
[Diego] <i>Dad, your longtime dream</i>
<i>is finally coming true.</i>

42
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:54,572
<i>Arnaldo and I will live as a family now.</i>

43
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:56,950
<i>We love you very much.</i>

44
00:02:01,454 --> 00:02:02,747
Stop the funeral!

45
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:06,167
Stop the funeral! Get out of my way!

46
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:08,336
Step aside! Let me through!

47
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:11,756
I'll bury my husband myself!
Stop the funeral!

48
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:15,677
Get out of here!
I will bury my own husband!

49
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,011
Emilia, that's enough.

50
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:19,305
-Get out of here!
-Don't make a scene!

51
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:20,515
Out!

52
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:24,060
I'm his wife so I should
bury him myself! Now get lost!

53
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:26,271
Ma, what are you doing?
Show Dad some respect.

54
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:28,857
How dare you go against your own mother?!

55
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,275
Did you hit your head again?

56
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,485
Want me to tell everyone
the truth about you?!

57
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:38,074
-Huh?! You want that?!
-Emilia! Stop it!

58
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:40,702
Why, Papa? Is everything my fault again?!

59
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:43,413
Will you kick me out
of my own husband's burial?

60
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:46,624
My husband's bastard son
should leave, not me!

61
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:49,544
And you! You killed my mother!

62
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:52,964
And you! You're just his wannabe mistress!

63
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:55,300
It's you who shouldn't be here! Get lost!

64
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:58,094
Don't blame us for what you did, Emilia!

65
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:00,889
I saw how you were the one who shot Raul.

66
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:03,600
I didn't kill him. I loved my husband.

67
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:06,686
Now, get out of my sight! Get lost!

68
00:03:07,145 --> 00:03:11,482
Don't you dare hurt my mother!
We didn't kill Raul, you did!

69
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,359
Go to hell!

70
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:16,654
Do you really want to bury your husband?

71
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:20,283
Fine. Then go rest in peace!

72
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:27,165
[crowd screams]

73
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:35,340
Get me out of here!

74
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:39,510
Let's go. Mom! Come on, Mom.

75
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:41,888
-Excuse us. Let us through!
-Help!

76
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:50,730
[grunting]

77
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:54,400
What did I tell you?

78
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:57,528
You keep picking fights
you can't even win.

79
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,863
Look at you!

80
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:01,282
You! Help her.

81
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:02,867
-Help! Faster!
-Get her out of there.

82
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:12,627
[sobs]

83
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,058
[yelps]

84
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:34,565
What the hell was that?
You are so dumb! You're stupid!

85
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:39,028
You know, I'm running
out of derogatory words

86
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:41,656
to explain your stupidity.

87
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:44,158
Hey, I'm not dumb! I'm smart!

88
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:48,037
-Hold that woman down. Now.
-Let go of me! Let go!

89
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:50,164
You think you're smart, don't you?

90
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,250
What did you do there, huh?

91
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,961
You made a laughingstock out of yourself!

92
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:57,672
You fell into the grave
because of your nonsense.

93
00:04:57,755 --> 00:04:59,173
You couldn't even defend yourself.

94
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:03,303
Not only that, you even
put Arnaldo in danger.

95
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,306
You're going to blow his cover!

96
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:09,600
Do you realize what Lily Cruz
could do to him

97
00:05:09,684 --> 00:05:12,478
once she learns that he's a spy?

98
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:16,941
You might just have to bury your son next!

99
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:19,152
You want that? You want that for Arnaldo?

100
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:23,531
Grandpa, I think Mama isn't
thinking clearly anymore.

101
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:26,034
We better go before
Lily suspects something.

102
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:27,535
You're right.

103
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:29,287
-Hey, stop--Hold her down!
-Let go of me!

104
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:32,623
-Don't let her go.
-Hold her. Get her in the car.

105
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,168
Get her in the car.
Come on, get her inside.

106
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:39,797
-Go!
-[Emilia screams]

107
00:05:42,675 --> 00:05:43,926
I hate you!

108
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:46,179
[Emilia sobs]

109
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:52,602
Stupid.

110
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:56,355
Let go of me! I'm not crazy!

111
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:58,566
Papa, why are you taking me here?

112
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,485
Please hold her down.

113
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:03,571
Wait, Papa. I don't belong here.

114
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:06,199
Stop it! Let go of me! Stop this!

115
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:09,994
Let go of me! Hey!
Why are you bringing me here?

116
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:12,288
Mama's going to get mad once she finds out

117
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:15,041
that you brought me here.
She'll tear you to pieces.

118
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:17,043
This is what's best for us, Emilia.

119
00:06:17,126 --> 00:06:19,587
Your lunacy isn't doing us
any good anymore.

120
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:22,465
How could you do this to me,
Papa? Let go of me!

121
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:24,509
Take that woman inside. Take her inside!

122
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,594
[screams]

123
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:27,762
Let go of me!

124
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:29,555
Let go of me!

125
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:33,601
Stop it! You're all going to regret this.

126
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:36,813
Hey, let go of me! You too!

127
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:38,731
Papa!

128
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:43,111
Papa, don't do this to me!
I don't deserve to be here!

129
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:48,574
Mama. Come on, please do something.

130
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:53,955
Look at what Papa's doing to me!
Mama, please!

131
00:06:55,706 --> 00:06:56,749
Raul?

132
00:06:57,542 --> 00:07:00,628
Raul, can you please--Raul.
Don't just stand there.

133
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:01,796
Do something!

134
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:07,677
What?!

135
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:12,515
Mama. Why am I here?

136
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:16,352
I don't deserve to be here, right?

137
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,271
Come on, Mama.

138
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:25,862
Raul? Raul, please.

139
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:28,406
Please, Raul.

140
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:34,787
Papa's at it again!
He's always doing this to me.

141
00:07:51,053 --> 00:07:52,763
Grandpa, are you okay?

142
00:07:53,556 --> 00:07:54,765
I'm fine, I'm fine.

143
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:03,649
Arnaldo, listen to me
and listen to me well.

144
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:07,153
We can't rely on your mother anymore.

145
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:10,114
It's just the two of us now.

146
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:15,995
It's up to us to reclaim
our family's lost glory.

147
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:19,290
Okay. But how are we going to do that?

148
00:08:19,373 --> 00:08:20,500
We lost a lot

149
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:23,294
since the kidnapping
turned into a major disaster.

150
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:25,087
Forget the kidnapping.

151
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:28,591
What matters is that we will be able

152
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:31,886
to take over Red Dragon's syndicate.

153
00:08:31,969 --> 00:08:35,598
That's the only way
for us to recover our lost power.

154
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:40,228
For us to get more men,
secure more weapons,

155
00:08:40,311 --> 00:08:43,689
more than enough money, and protection.

156
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:47,443
And your grandma's syndicate
could provide all that.

157
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,362
That's exactly what we need.

158
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:51,864
All right. I'm all in.

159
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,659
But you have to promise me one thing.

160
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:56,911
Lily Cruz is mine.

161
00:08:58,246 --> 00:09:01,082
She's going to be my slave,
and I want Diego dead.

162
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:02,667
You understand?

163
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:05,795
Help me, then.

164
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:10,174
Help me get your grandma's fortune,

165
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:12,093
and I promise you,

166
00:09:12,176 --> 00:09:17,848
I will give you Lily Cruz
and Diego on a silver platter.

167
00:09:18,891 --> 00:09:21,227
[ominous music swelling]

168
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:35,408
Lily Cruz had my wife
and daughter kidnapped.

169
00:09:36,158 --> 00:09:39,620
And two members of my family
died because of them.

170
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:45,501
<i>My daughter, Emilia,</i>
<i>did not kill her husband, Raul.</i>

171
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:49,672
<i>Lily Cruz killed Raul and Helena.</i>

172
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:54,927
<i>Helena died while trying</i>
<i>to save our daughter, Emilia.</i>

173
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:56,679
She died a hero.

174
00:09:58,055 --> 00:09:59,390
But Lily Cruz?

175
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:03,185
She's the real Red Dragon.

176
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,732
<i>She's the real criminal!</i>

177
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:13,696
And I swear by the name
of my beloved, Helena.

178
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:16,907
Helena, if you're listening up in heaven…

179
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:22,913
<i>I promise you that I won't stop</i>
<i>until that criminal, Lily Cruz,</i>

180
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:25,291
<i>pays for all her crimes.</i>

181
00:10:26,542 --> 00:10:30,630
Governor, what do you have
to say about Jaguar's claim

182
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:33,174
that you were part
of Red Dragon's syndicate?

183
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:35,301
And that you allegedly had Lily Cruz

184
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:36,969
and her mother kidnapped?

185
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:40,473
<i>These are all lies.</i>

186
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:43,601
<i>Let's just see</i>
<i>who the people will believe.</i>

187
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:46,395
<i>A criminal like Damian,</i>

188
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:50,900
<i>or their trusted Governor Julio?</i>

189
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,874
And there he goes again.
Lying straight to our faces.

190
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:10,378
Hey! Stop badmouthing the Ardientes.

191
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:12,129
Why? I'm telling the truth.

192
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:15,174
If someone hears you,
they might have you kidnapped.

193
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:17,593
Do you want to end up like Lily Cruz?

194
00:11:20,679 --> 00:11:23,307
Mr. Damian, what can you say?

195
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:25,768
Mr. Damian, please give us a statement.

196
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,359
<i>Don't believe Julio Ardiente.</i>

197
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:35,903
I am the Jaguar.

198
00:11:36,654 --> 00:11:39,156
I used to work for Red Dragon.

199
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,825
I know what really happened.

200
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:44,870
Who is the real Red Dragon,
Helena Montoya or Lily Cruz?

201
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:47,832
Helena Montoya was Red Dragon.

202
00:11:48,332 --> 00:11:50,042
<i>She had control over the syndicates</i>

203
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:52,169
<i>and connections to the Triad.</i>

204
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:55,589
She also worked with the Ardientes.

205
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:59,593
They were the ones who
kidnapped Lily and Camia Cruz.

206
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:02,471
Damian Cruz, why did you turn yourself in?

207
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:09,562
I surrendered because I don't
want to hurt the people I love.

208
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:12,940
<i>They've given me countless chances.</i>

209
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:15,151
<i>I don't want to disappoint them again.</i>

210
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:21,490
<i>I will get my life together</i>
<i>because I want to be worthy</i>

211
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,993
<i>of the love they have shown me.</i>

212
00:12:26,662 --> 00:12:29,415
[tense music playing]

213
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:50,853
<i>Helena died while trying</i>
<i>to save our daughter, Emilia.</i>

214
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:54,064
<i>She died a hero. But Lily Cruz?</i>

215
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:58,777
<i>She's the real Red Dragon.</i>
<i>She's the real criminal!</i>

216
00:13:00,321 --> 00:13:02,531
<i>Helena, if you're listening up in heaven,</i>

217
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:07,661
<i>I promise you that I won't stop</i>
<i>until that criminal, Lily Cruz,</i>

218
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,581
<i>pays for all her crimes.</i>

219
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:27,223
Lily…

220
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:31,060
Mom.

221
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:32,645
I just found out that Julio

222
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:35,689
had Emilia sent to a psychiatric ward.

223
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:37,358
[chuckles]

224
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:39,860
That's where that woman belongs.

225
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,654
And I'm not surprised, Mom.

226
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:44,406
Because all the Ardientes are insane.

227
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:47,660
So, that's why Emilia wasn't
at the press conference.

228
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:48,744
[scoffs]

229
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:50,579
Can you believe it?

230
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,333
Julio was able to do that
to his own daughter.

231
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:59,171
Julio Ardiente? I expect nothing less.

232
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:02,424
The Ardientes don't care about family.

233
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:03,968
And I have a strong feeling

234
00:14:04,051 --> 00:14:07,680
that Julio had something to do
with Helena's death.

235
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,182
Now, the question is…

236
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:15,646
Who's helping him take over

237
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:20,150
Red Dragon's position in the syndicate?

238
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:39,295
[ominous music playing]

239
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:53,475
<i>Arnaldo!</i>

240
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:56,478
<i>For tonight's entertainment.</i>

241
00:14:56,854 --> 00:14:59,148
<i>My Lily Cruz. Choose.</i>

242
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:01,442
<i>-What do you want? This one?</i>
<i>-Let me go.</i>

243
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:02,943
<i>This one? No. I'll pick.</i>

244
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:04,194
[yelps]

245
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:06,071
<i>You want it? Tell me you want more.</i>

246
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:07,865
<i>-Want more?</i>
<i>-You bastard!</i>

247
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:10,117
<i>Yes! Yes!</i>

248
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:13,203
<i>-You bastard!</i>
<i>-You love me?</i>

249
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,164
<i>-No, I don't love you!</i>
<i>-You love me!</i>

250
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:18,792
<i>Here's more!</i>

251
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:28,218
<i>Don't come near me.</i>

252
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:35,184
<i>Arnaldo!</i>

253
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:45,361
[tense music playing]

254
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:07,925
[ominous music playing]

255
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:14,056
<i>How dare you go against your own mother?!</i>

256
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:15,516
<i>Did you hit your head again?</i>

257
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:17,851
<i>Want me to tell everyone</i>
<i>the truth about you?! Huh?!</i>

258
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:25,234
<i>-You want that?!</i>
<i>-Emilia! Stop it!</i>

259
00:16:25,734 --> 00:16:27,861
<i>Why, Papa? Is everything my fault again?!</i>

260
00:16:27,945 --> 00:16:30,572
<i>Will you kick me out of</i>
<i>my own husband's burial?</i>

261
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:40,457
<i>The real Arnaldo's back.</i>
<i>He's the one helping Julio.</i>

262
00:16:46,171 --> 00:16:47,172
Diego.

263
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:50,467
Diego.

264
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:56,015
When will all this end?

265
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:01,145
I really thought Arnaldo changed.

266
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:06,942
What next? I have nothing left.

267
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,861
They've already taken
everything away from me.

268
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,155
No. I'm here.

269
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:13,699
I'm still here.

270
00:17:14,616 --> 00:17:20,080
We are all here for you.
We're your family now, Diego.

271
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:25,753
Lily, come with me.

272
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:29,131
Let's run away from here. Far away.

273
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:32,259
Let's fulfill our dreams.

274
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:37,681
I want to be a father and a husband.

275
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:41,310
I want us to start our
own family and live in peace.

276
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:46,315
Lily, now's our chance
to finally be happy.

277
00:17:58,202 --> 00:17:59,286
[car honks]

278
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:23,310
[soft instrumental playing]

279
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:44,248
[soft instrumental playing]

280
00:19:01,056 --> 00:19:04,768
Well. Our house hasn't changed.

281
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:05,936
[Julio chuckles]

282
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,412
It hasn't changed at all.

283
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:27,207
Just like the way we left it.

284
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:31,503
You smell that?

285
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:36,884
Ah, the scent of power.

286
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:38,760
[chuckles]

287
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:44,433
Well, it's good to be home.

288
00:19:47,352 --> 00:19:52,858
This place was where I shaped
who you'd become.

289
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:58,071
This is where I shaped you to be a ruler.

290
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:03,368
So, it's only fitting that this is where

291
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:09,124
the Ardiente family should start over.

292
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:14,880
And in no time, we will reign
over this town again.

293
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:18,675
Well, if that is the case,
I better get going.

294
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:20,177
I'm meeting with Lily.

295
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,679
I must find out if our enemies

296
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:25,849
are planning something against you again.

297
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:28,310
So, you mean to tell me

298
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:30,812
that you know
where Lily Cruz's new house is?

299
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:33,273
Yes. It wasn't that hard to find.

300
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:34,858
[chuckles]

301
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:42,282
You know, I don't think
they're hiding from us.

302
00:20:43,116 --> 00:20:45,410
I think they've accepted the fact

303
00:20:46,036 --> 00:20:48,664
that they can never escape us.

304
00:20:49,206 --> 00:20:53,710
Perhaps they're running away
from the nightmares

305
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:57,506
they had in their old house because of us.

306
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,384
Well, I guess it's time we tormented them

307
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:02,886
with a new nightmare.

308
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:04,471
Don't you agree?

309
00:21:04,846 --> 00:21:05,889
Okay.

310
00:21:06,848 --> 00:21:10,519
Just be careful at all times, Arnaldo.

311
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:14,940
I don't want anything bad
to happen to you.

312
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:21,571
I cannot afford anything bad
to happen to you.

313
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,073
Understand?

314
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:26,743
Viva Ardiente.

315
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:28,287
Viva Ardiente.

316
00:21:41,466 --> 00:21:44,261
[soft instrumental playing]

317
00:22:01,361 --> 00:22:03,322
Put all the luggage in the trunk, okay?

318
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:06,825
We have to leave before anyone sees us.

319
00:22:07,242 --> 00:22:09,619
[ominous music playing]

320
00:22:18,628 --> 00:22:19,504
Let's go.

321
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:21,006
Ma'am, where are we going again?

322
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:25,260
To the St. Monica chapel in Rosario.

323
00:22:25,343 --> 00:22:28,513
Lily has strictly ordered us not to
let anyone know we're leaving.

324
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:30,015
How come?

325
00:22:30,557 --> 00:22:33,310
I have no idea. Shall we?

326
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:34,936
-Okay.
-Let's go.

327
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:42,110
[ominous music playing]

328
00:22:52,662 --> 00:22:58,668
Well, hello there.
What are you guys up to?

329
00:23:09,971 --> 00:23:12,516
Governor, your visitors are here.

330
00:23:15,143 --> 00:23:16,645
Hello, ladies.

331
00:23:18,021 --> 00:23:19,689
Please sit down.

332
00:23:21,858 --> 00:23:24,569
Ah, Jenny, could you prepare us
some hors d'oeuvres

333
00:23:24,653 --> 00:23:26,071
and a bottle of wine?

334
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:31,493
Oh, I didn't get your name.

335
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:33,954
-Cris.
-Hello, Cris.

336
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:38,291
So, you want to take control
of Red Dragon's syndicate?

337
00:23:39,084 --> 00:23:44,464
Yes. I'd like to get her money,
her resources,

338
00:23:45,382 --> 00:23:46,550
her arms…

339
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:48,885
All her businesses.

340
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:52,889
With all due respect, Governor,
but what's in it for us?

341
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:55,183
The Ardientes are ruined.

342
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:58,395
You're running out of men
and what's left of your funds.

343
00:23:59,229 --> 00:24:02,649
The only thing you have left
is your position.

344
00:24:04,234 --> 00:24:06,736
Don't underestimate my position, Cris.

345
00:24:08,196 --> 00:24:11,241
I'm still the governor of this province.

346
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:16,204
Now, let's look at the other side.

347
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,581
Let's take a look at your group.

348
00:24:17,956 --> 00:24:21,585
The other syndicates are slowly
starting to consume you.

349
00:24:21,668 --> 00:24:24,212
And I'm aware that the police
are on your tail.

350
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:28,008
You're like frightened little mice

351
00:24:28,091 --> 00:24:31,094
scurrying blind all over the place.

352
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:33,513
What you need now

353
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:38,727
is a new leader to lead your syndicate.

354
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:43,064
And I'm the only one who can do that.

355
00:24:44,357 --> 00:24:45,442
So, you see?

356
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:50,822
You need me as much as I need you.

357
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:53,074
No deal.

358
00:24:54,659 --> 00:24:56,828
If you want to take over
Red Dragon's group,

359
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:58,997
we aren't the ones
you should be talking to.

360
00:25:00,373 --> 00:25:01,499
Then, who?

361
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,293
The lords of the syndicate.

362
00:25:03,668 --> 00:25:05,170
[laughs]

363
00:25:05,253 --> 00:25:08,548
So, there's someone higher than Helena?

364
00:25:09,591 --> 00:25:10,550
The Triad.

365
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:16,556
[tense music playing]

366
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:38,161
[tense music playing]

367
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:46,378
We can only allow one companion
for Governor Ardiente.

368
00:25:47,629 --> 00:25:49,214
Stay here, I'll go with him.

369
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:04,521
[ominous music playing]

370
00:26:15,657 --> 00:26:16,658
Jepoy?

371
00:26:17,575 --> 00:26:19,119
-Ma'am?
-I think we're being followed.

372
00:26:28,169 --> 00:26:29,629
Is it Julio's men?

373
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:34,259
We have to lose them, Jepoy. Hurry.

374
00:26:34,342 --> 00:26:35,635
All right. Hold on.

375
00:26:43,393 --> 00:26:48,106
You can't run from me.
You can't run from me.

376
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:57,657
[ominous music playing]

377
00:27:01,328 --> 00:27:03,788
Jepoy, they're still behind us.
We need to lose them.

378
00:27:17,218 --> 00:27:19,346
[tense music playing]

379
00:27:25,268 --> 00:27:26,728
Jepoy, watch out for that truck!

380
00:27:30,648 --> 00:27:31,941
[tires screeching]

381
00:27:43,828 --> 00:27:45,789
[tires screeching]

382
00:27:59,177 --> 00:28:00,595
Hey! Watch where you're going!

383
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:02,389
What did you say?!

384
00:28:07,811 --> 00:28:10,063
[breathing heavily]

385
00:28:15,235 --> 00:28:16,236
[grunts]

386
00:28:30,583 --> 00:28:31,751
No!

387
00:28:33,628 --> 00:28:35,839
[breathing heavily]

388
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:42,804
<i>You can run, but you can't hide.</i>
<i>I'll find out what you're up to.</i>

389
00:28:56,359 --> 00:28:59,237
Governor Julio Ardiente.

390
00:29:01,114 --> 00:29:02,657
Stefano dela Torre.

391
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:07,078
I represent the Triad.

392
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:18,798
I assure you the whole province
of Ardiente

393
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:20,967
will be under my control

394
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:25,638
if I can take over
Helena Montoya's organization.

395
00:29:26,681 --> 00:29:27,682
[scoffs]

396
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:32,562
And what makes you think
we'll hand it over to you?

397
00:29:34,564 --> 00:29:39,652
Well, I am the only ally
of Helena in Ardiente.

398
00:29:40,570 --> 00:29:41,988
So, it's only right

399
00:29:42,071 --> 00:29:47,160
that I take over her syndicate
in my province.

400
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:51,498
Then give me the password.

401
00:29:52,582 --> 00:29:53,583
What?

402
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:56,878
If you and Red Dragon really were allies,

403
00:29:58,671 --> 00:30:01,508
then she would've given you
the password already.

404
00:30:18,107 --> 00:30:19,442
Where's my daughter?

405
00:30:19,526 --> 00:30:21,194
She asked me to give you this, ma'am.

406
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:23,404
-Huh?
-To all of you.

407
00:30:54,686 --> 00:30:57,564
For you to gain access
to the Triad's database.

408
00:30:58,523 --> 00:31:02,151
Or perhaps, she only toyed with you,

409
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:06,281
the same way she deceived other
politicians and businessmen.

410
00:31:08,491 --> 00:31:09,659
Without the password,

411
00:31:12,328 --> 00:31:15,582
I cannot give you the resources
and the protection

412
00:31:15,665 --> 00:31:17,041
that you are asking for.

413
00:31:22,672 --> 00:31:24,173
And without the password…

414
00:31:28,261 --> 00:31:30,054
We cannot trust you.

415
00:31:36,477 --> 00:31:40,565
Good day, Governor Ardiente.

416
00:32:06,299 --> 00:32:07,300
Mom?

417
00:32:08,259 --> 00:32:09,260
Lily!

418
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:17,685
Lily, Diego, what's this?

419
00:32:19,354 --> 00:32:20,355
Mom.

420
00:32:22,148 --> 00:32:25,860
Starting tomorrow, I will be Diego's wife.

421
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:27,487
We're getting married.

422
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:40,875
Oh, Lily!

423
00:32:51,469 --> 00:32:54,055
We've prepared your suits and dresses.

424
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:59,394
I'm so happy for you both. Finally!

425
00:33:16,744 --> 00:33:18,371
[Stefano] <i>If you and Red Dragon</i>
<i>really were allies,</i>

426
00:33:18,454 --> 00:33:21,290
<i>then she would've given you</i>
<i>the password already.</i>

427
00:33:21,374 --> 00:33:24,168
<i>For you to gain access</i>
<i>to the Triad's database.</i>

428
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:26,629
<i>Or perhaps, she only toyed with you,</i>

429
00:33:26,713 --> 00:33:29,966
<i>the same way she deceived other</i>
<i>politicians and businessmen.</i>

430
00:33:30,466 --> 00:33:33,594
<i>Without the password,</i>
<i>I cannot give you the resources</i>

431
00:33:33,678 --> 00:33:35,763
<i>and the protection</i>
<i>that you are asking for.</i>

432
00:33:37,265 --> 00:33:42,478
<i>You can't deceive me, Helena.</i>
<i>A woman can never deceive me.</i>

433
00:33:53,406 --> 00:33:54,490
Colonel.

434
00:34:06,085 --> 00:34:08,963
You're all set, Governor.
You can go inside now.

435
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:12,675
-Colonel, wait for me here.
-Yes, Governor.

436
00:34:15,970 --> 00:34:18,681
[humming]

437
00:34:32,028 --> 00:34:34,572
Hi, Papa. Look. I'm practicing the piano.

438
00:34:35,239 --> 00:34:37,784
[humming]

439
00:34:44,749 --> 00:34:45,708
Emilia.

440
00:34:47,126 --> 00:34:48,211
That's enough.

441
00:34:50,671 --> 00:34:52,090
Your mother's dead.

442
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:55,134
That's not true, Papa.

443
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:58,679
Mama just told me
that she's on her way here.

444
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:02,016
You know, she's going to see me
because she misses me so much.

445
00:35:03,810 --> 00:35:08,564
It sounds like you
and your mother really bonded.

446
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:10,358
Of course, Papa.

447
00:35:10,441 --> 00:35:14,695
In that short time,
I really felt loved, Papa.

448
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:18,241
Mama really loves me.
She gave me almost everything.

449
00:35:18,324 --> 00:35:21,536
Money, power, everything, Papa.

450
00:35:21,619 --> 00:35:24,372
But more importantly, the trust.

451
00:35:24,455 --> 00:35:27,083
So, I really feel that,
you know, Mama loves me.

452
00:35:27,166 --> 00:35:29,293
[humming]

453
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:35,716
Did she ever mention to you
about the syndicate?

454
00:35:36,884 --> 00:35:39,512
Yes, she told me that I would inherit it.

455
00:35:39,929 --> 00:35:41,806
Because I'm the heiress to the throne.

456
00:35:42,473 --> 00:35:44,767
[humming]

457
00:35:45,685 --> 00:35:50,773
Did she give you the Triad's password?

458
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:55,987
[humming]

459
00:36:00,116 --> 00:36:01,159
Emilia.

460
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:07,582
I need that password,

461
00:36:09,876 --> 00:36:15,173
so I can take over
your mother's syndicate.

462
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:23,973
[tense music playing]

463
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:52,251
[humming frantically]

464
00:36:54,378 --> 00:36:56,214
Emilia, please stop it!

465
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:58,716
-Stop it!
-Ah!

466
00:36:58,799 --> 00:37:01,177
-Papa, what are you doing?
-Give me the password!

467
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:04,138
Give me the password!
Give me the password!

468
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:06,974
-Ow!
-Give it to me!

469
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:11,354
[sobbing]

470
00:37:46,013 --> 00:37:47,014
Diego?

471
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:50,309
Why are you still here?

472
00:37:55,314 --> 00:37:57,149
LI'L BRO, WHAT'S UP?

473
00:38:01,821 --> 00:38:03,364
What do you feel about this?

474
00:38:03,906 --> 00:38:07,910
Are you feeling guilty that
you didn't invite Arnaldo?

475
00:38:09,662 --> 00:38:11,455
Lily, what if we're wrong?

476
00:38:13,457 --> 00:38:15,376
What if Arnaldo really has changed?

477
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:25,219
So, you're willing to risk
our lives for him?

478
00:38:26,595 --> 00:38:28,597
Are you really willing
to risk our dreams, Diego?

479
00:38:37,273 --> 00:38:39,400
I'm willing to give up everything for you.

480
00:38:41,694 --> 00:38:42,903
I love you.

481
00:38:54,457 --> 00:38:55,458
Hey!

482
00:38:58,294 --> 00:39:00,296
-Oh, my.
-Mom.

483
00:39:00,379 --> 00:39:01,839
Look at you two.

484
00:39:02,757 --> 00:39:05,468
The bride and groom mustn't see each other

485
00:39:05,551 --> 00:39:08,804
the night before the wedding.
That's bad luck, you know?

486
00:39:09,764 --> 00:39:13,017
Sorry, Mom. It's Diego's fault.

487
00:39:13,100 --> 00:39:15,186
He didn't want to go inside just yet.

488
00:39:16,687 --> 00:39:18,230
Auntie, I can't wait.

489
00:39:19,565 --> 00:39:22,735
I'm so excited to start
my new life with my wife.

490
00:39:23,819 --> 00:39:25,654
Diego, just a little longer.

491
00:39:26,447 --> 00:39:28,783
And all your dreams will come true.

492
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:34,372
-Just a bit more.
-It'll happen tomorrow.

493
00:39:34,455 --> 00:39:37,500
-Now, go on. Go on inside.
-You heard your fiancée.

494
00:39:39,168 --> 00:39:40,127
All right.

495
00:39:41,045 --> 00:39:42,380
But where's my good night kiss?

496
00:39:42,838 --> 00:39:44,673
In front of my mom? Are you serious?

497
00:39:44,757 --> 00:39:46,884
Tomorrow, then. Good night.

498
00:39:48,302 --> 00:39:50,471
-Good night kiss.
-Still trying to score.

499
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:58,938
I still don't have any updates
on Lily and Diego.

500
00:39:59,855 --> 00:40:01,148
But if my hunch is right,

501
00:40:01,232 --> 00:40:03,401
they're planning something against you.

502
00:40:03,901 --> 00:40:08,656
Well, I want you to take care of that.

503
00:40:09,657 --> 00:40:12,201
Because my plate is full.

504
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:15,830
Your mom's weirdness and incompetence

505
00:40:15,913 --> 00:40:18,082
are the roots of all my problems.

506
00:40:18,958 --> 00:40:20,751
I don't know. I think she was born

507
00:40:20,835 --> 00:40:23,587
to be a total pain in the neck.

508
00:40:24,255 --> 00:40:25,631
I've got a migraine.

509
00:40:27,466 --> 00:40:28,676
-Grandpa.
-Yeah?

510
00:40:30,719 --> 00:40:33,180
I need you to relax, okay?

511
00:40:33,472 --> 00:40:35,683
Too much worrying is bad for your health.

512
00:40:36,684 --> 00:40:37,893
I'll take care of it.

513
00:40:41,897 --> 00:40:46,569
Arnaldo, I want to clear a path
for your comeback.

514
00:40:47,653 --> 00:40:51,657
So that you can fulfill
all of your lifelong dreams.

515
00:40:54,660 --> 00:40:58,497
And let's face it. Let's face the truth.

516
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:01,333
Age is creeping up on me.

517
00:41:02,042 --> 00:41:04,253
I'm starting to feel it in my body.

518
00:41:04,336 --> 00:41:07,214
I'm feeling it in my bones.

519
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:13,304
And I'm ready to turn over
the baton of leadership to you.

520
00:41:15,389 --> 00:41:20,895
You know, I would be willing
to give up everything

521
00:41:20,978 --> 00:41:24,607
just to see you lead this town

522
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:30,863
and continue our legacy,
the legacy of our family.

523
00:41:31,739 --> 00:41:33,574
That is how it is going to be.

524
00:41:34,909 --> 00:41:38,204
That is how the future will turn out.

525
00:41:38,913 --> 00:41:43,417
But what they don't see is how
much you protect this family,

526
00:41:44,043 --> 00:41:46,212
how you take care of us. How…

527
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:52,092
-How much you love me and Mama.
-That's true.

528
00:41:53,427 --> 00:41:54,553
And in truth…

529
00:41:57,389 --> 00:42:00,684
In truth, you are the best thing
that ever happened to me.

530
00:42:02,811 --> 00:42:05,564
I want you to know that
I'll do everything in my power

531
00:42:05,648 --> 00:42:09,109
to… protect you.

532
00:42:09,193 --> 00:42:10,819
Take care of you.

533
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:14,573
Just a little longer,

534
00:42:16,450 --> 00:42:19,495
I'll be the one
carrying on the family's legacy.

535
00:42:20,454 --> 00:42:21,789
I promise you that.

536
00:42:22,665 --> 00:42:27,962
That has always been my dream.
Thank you so much.

537
00:42:30,589 --> 00:42:34,301
You know, Lily, your father always wanted

538
00:42:34,718 --> 00:42:37,429
to walk you down the aisle
at your wedding.

539
00:42:39,932 --> 00:42:41,892
But on one condition.

540
00:42:42,851 --> 00:42:44,812
You'll only get married once you're forty.

541
00:42:44,895 --> 00:42:46,355
[laughs]

542
00:42:48,232 --> 00:42:50,317
Well, Dad, I'm sorry.

543
00:42:51,569 --> 00:42:55,322
I'll get married thirteen years early.

544
00:42:58,284 --> 00:43:00,077
Still, Lily.

545
00:43:01,495 --> 00:43:04,206
I just know he's smiling
down on you right now.

546
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:07,501
Because you've found
your better half in Diego.

547
00:43:11,714 --> 00:43:13,090
I hope so, Mom.

548
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,685
[laughs]

549
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:37,031
I want your men
to search Poblacion Ardiente

550
00:43:37,114 --> 00:43:39,408
for a white van with this plate number.

551
00:43:41,785 --> 00:43:43,787
And I want results
first thing in the morning.

552
00:43:45,122 --> 00:43:46,290
Will do, Mayor.

553
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:49,126
Okay.

554
00:43:52,671 --> 00:43:53,672
Let's go.

555
00:44:04,475 --> 00:44:05,934
Arnaldo!

556
00:44:07,102 --> 00:44:08,646
What took you so long?

557
00:44:08,729 --> 00:44:11,231
I've been waiting so long
for you to visit me.

558
00:44:11,774 --> 00:44:14,360
Hey, look. Those are my constituents.

559
00:44:14,443 --> 00:44:17,237
Please say hi to them.
Look, it's the mayor.

560
00:44:18,656 --> 00:44:24,161
Ah, sorry. I've been busy.

561
00:44:24,244 --> 00:44:27,122
What happened to you? Tell me.

562
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:29,249
Your grandfather beat me up.

563
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:34,797
Why is he so cruel to me?
It's like I'm not his daughter.

564
00:44:35,964 --> 00:44:39,677
Well, it's because you always
give him a hard time.

565
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:43,681
Listen.

566
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:48,143
I'll be gone for a while.

567
00:44:49,436 --> 00:44:52,231
-You're leaving?
-Yeah.

568
00:44:53,107 --> 00:44:54,775
I'm going to look for Lily and Diego.

569
00:44:56,652 --> 00:45:00,364
So, it'll be just you
and Grandpa for a while.

570
00:45:02,032 --> 00:45:03,742
But you have to promise me one thing.

571
00:45:05,452 --> 00:45:06,745
Don't fight anymore.

572
00:45:08,455 --> 00:45:09,456
Okay?

573
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:14,086
It's easy. Just give him what he wants.

574
00:45:16,463 --> 00:45:17,881
And, just to give you a tip,

575
00:45:18,966 --> 00:45:22,594
help him take over grandma's syndicate

576
00:45:22,678 --> 00:45:24,012
and everything will be fine.

577
00:45:27,766 --> 00:45:33,147
It's not fair. Your grandma
and papa already left me.

578
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:37,025
And now, you're leaving.
I'll be all alone.

579
00:45:37,734 --> 00:45:42,239
Can you just stay, please?
Don't leave. Please.

580
00:45:45,367 --> 00:45:46,660
I have to go.

581
00:45:48,537 --> 00:45:49,788
I have to.

582
00:45:51,206 --> 00:45:55,836
I'm really sorry I wasn't
a very good mother to you.

583
00:45:57,754 --> 00:45:59,756
You could've been a great man

584
00:45:59,840 --> 00:46:02,176
if only I'd just raised you properly.

585
00:46:04,219 --> 00:46:07,431
But no matter what other people
say about us,

586
00:46:07,514 --> 00:46:10,434
that our family's crazy,
or that we're evil,

587
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:15,564
believe me when I say
that I really love you.

588
00:46:15,647 --> 00:46:19,735
And no one can question that.
I love you so much, son.

589
00:46:27,034 --> 00:46:28,202
I love you too.

590
00:46:29,828 --> 00:46:31,663
I love you too. I love you too.

591
00:46:32,956 --> 00:46:35,709
[Emilia sobs]

592
00:46:36,668 --> 00:46:38,670
I love you too, son.

593
00:46:39,880 --> 00:46:43,967
My son. I love you so much.

594
00:46:47,721 --> 00:46:48,764
I have to go.

595
00:46:50,474 --> 00:46:51,683
I have to go.

596
00:47:01,735 --> 00:47:02,736
Arnaldo.

597
00:47:04,238 --> 00:47:09,451
Um, if you see your grandma and your papa,

598
00:47:09,535 --> 00:47:13,497
can you please say hi to them for me?

599
00:47:14,456 --> 00:47:16,625
Tell them I miss them so much.

600
00:47:17,084 --> 00:47:19,836
You know, they're just
somewhere out there.

601
00:47:21,004 --> 00:47:22,005
Huh?

602
00:47:23,549 --> 00:47:25,801
[Emilia giggles]

603
00:47:37,354 --> 00:47:40,274
Hey, hang that properly. It's crooked.

604
00:47:42,109 --> 00:47:45,153
A little to the left.
A little more. There.

605
00:47:45,237 --> 00:47:48,282
Good. Okay.

606
00:47:50,242 --> 00:47:52,995
Now take the other paintings out with you.

607
00:47:59,459 --> 00:48:00,460
[chuckles]

608
00:48:15,267 --> 00:48:19,021
<i>I won't allow this family's reign to end.</i>

609
00:48:21,732 --> 00:48:26,612
<i>And you, Arnaldo, will continue my legacy.</i>

610
00:48:32,034 --> 00:48:35,495
<i>You are the future of the Ardiente clan.</i>

611
00:48:37,331 --> 00:48:40,584
<i>Live long, my son. Live long.</i>

612
00:48:47,883 --> 00:48:50,177
[Diego] <i>Lily, no matter</i>
<i>how many times I fall,</i>

613
00:48:50,260 --> 00:48:52,387
<i>no matter how many times I get hurt,</i>

614
00:48:52,471 --> 00:48:54,306
<i>I'll never stop loving you.</i>

615
00:48:54,389 --> 00:48:57,559
<i>Diego, you're the reason</i>
<i>I learned to love again.</i>

616
00:48:57,643 --> 00:49:00,479
<i>Thank you for teaching me how to love.</i>

617
00:49:00,562 --> 00:49:03,565
<i>We've tracked them down. In Rosario.</i>

618
00:49:03,649 --> 00:49:05,359
<i>I offer you this ring</i>

619
00:49:05,442 --> 00:49:08,862
<i>as a symbol of my eternal love</i>
<i>and faithfulness to you.</i>

620
00:49:08,945 --> 00:49:14,034
<i>Wear this ring as a symbol</i>
<i>of my eternal love</i>

621
00:49:14,117 --> 00:49:15,994
<i>and faithfulness to you.</i>

622
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:23,126
[theme music playing]
